      "message": "OTA-1867 \u2014 the second disclosure is its own question\n\nSix authored vendor topics held TWO disclosures behind ONE label:\nirma_berrin, irma_nimari, halem_stayed, elara_ring, felra_stopped,\nnalren_why. Ask-once and a second answer cannot both be true \u2014 the second\npress is refused before the counter write \u2014 so after OTA-1866 those six\nsecond paragraphs were content no player could reach.\n\nOwner ruling: every visible vendor conversation question is ask-once, and\ndeeper conversation is a DISTINCT follow-up question, not the same question\nasked twice.\n\nTHE GATE. `TopicGate.requiresTopic` names a topic on the SAME person's set\nthat must already have been asked \u2014 the first gate dimension that asks about\nthe CONVERSATION rather than the world. It resolves through\n`conversationMemory(npcId, talked)`, a closure rather than the ledger, so the\ngate layer can ask exactly one thing and the answer still comes from\n`topicSpent`. Additive with every existing clause, and fail-closed: a context\ncarrying no conversation memory reads as \"nothing has been asked\", so a\nmissing ledger never OPENS a door.\n\nTHE OLD AUTHORITY IS DELETED, NOT DORMANT. `answersAvailable` was a branch \u2014\none answer for a laned person, `lines.length` for an authored one \u2014 and that\nbranch is what two readers drifted across for a year. It is now the constant\nANSWERS_PER_QUESTION, and no authored topic holds a second line. A class\nset's six lines remain PARALLEL VOICES inside one ask-once topic; that is\n`voiceLaneFor`'s business and was never a count of answers.\n\nTHE SAME CONVERSATION. `raiseTopic` re-derives the open list from `topicsFor`\nafter the counter write, against the faction the sheet opened with, so a\nfollow-up unlocked by an answer is askable without closing and reopening. It\nonly ever ADDS: a question the player can see must not vanish under their\nthumb.\n\nLEGACY IS A MIGRATION FIELD, NOT A RULE. A pre-split save can hold\n`<npc>:<parent> = 2`, meaning that player already heard disclosure 2.\n`Topic.legacyHeardWith` says so on those six rows, naming the exact old\nparent and the exact old count, read in one place. It is NOT \"a follow-up\ninherits its parent's count\" \u2014 that would be wrong for every ordinary\nfollow-up authored after today.\n\nCorpus 347 -> 353 topics, 41 sets unchanged; multi-line rows 12 -> 6, all six\nremaining being class:roadside voice lanes. All 12 authored paragraphs\nsurvive: six first paragraphs byte-identical, four second paragraphs edited\nonly where they claimed the player had asked the same question twice (41\ncharacters of 1,939).\n\n`talkContextFor` moved to app/state/talkContext.ts, body otherwise unchanged.\nIt was never store work \u2014 it takes a player and a world memory and returns a\nplain context \u2014 and gameStore.ts was at its ceiling. Ceiling 36815 -> 36812.\n\nNew suite ota1867TheSecondDisclosureIsItsOwnQuestion 31/31; five negative\ncontrols each detected their own class with production restored byte-for-byte\nafterwards. ota1866 24/24 and ota1784 20/20 green on the converted corpus.\n22/22 check gates, typecheck source clean, test ratchet at baseline 196, lint\nclean.\n\nNOT CLAIMED: nothing here changes non-vendor conversation, gameplay,\npresentation, crafting, grants, prices or navigation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LGFtzR6AQJbu4XdR28y3fX",
